# The idle loop's interrupt path without a timer: a test variant of the loop
# raises the spurious vector with `int 0xff`. Each time the frame is
# discarded, irq::handle runs with interrupts off, and the loop is entered
# again on a fresh stack, so every round sees the same RSP.
cmdline: test=idle_irq
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: idle: round 1: interrupt 0xff with IF 0 at RSP 0xffffffff8
expect: idle: round 2: interrupt 0xff with IF 0 at RSP 0xffffffff8
expect: idle: round 3: interrupt 0xff with IF 0 at RSP 0xffffffff8
expect: idle: 3 interrupts from the idle loop, each on a fresh stack
expect: TEST PASS
